{
    "about": "The shared cases of the deploy that the publishing tool starts after a push (issue 32, BUILD-02, PUB-42). Both faces read them: apps/plugin/src/publishing/deploy.spec.ts and cli/src/deploy.rs. \"commands\": the settings of a device (an empty text is a setting that is not set), whether the run is a takedown, and the command that the tool runs (the program, its arguments, and the folder where it runs), or the error of a deploy report that deploys nothing. \"windows\": true runs a case with the rule of Windows for an absolute path, else the rule of Unix. \"paths\": the one rule of an absolute path of both faces. \"results\": the exit code of the deploy (null: stopped by a signal), its standard output, and the deploy report that the tool gives, as the \"deployment\" object of its output (\"startError\": the deploy could not start, with this message of the system; \"takedown\": true for a deploy with --takedown; \"stopped\": the tool stopped the deploy after its time limit of \"timeoutMinutes\", or for the author). A time limit that the settings do not name is 30 minutes. A count of the result is a whole number from 0 in any form of JSON (1.0, 1e2, -0). A byte order mark at the start of a line is taken away, and a line of spaces and tabs only is blank. Every finished report has \"state\": \"done\". \"started\": the report of a deploy that starts in the background (the MCP server never waits for a build). \"last\": what the deploy tool and command give with last, from the text of the last report that the record of the device keeps (\"stored\", null for none) and whether a deploy runs.",
